-- title:
--   Scaling of a γ-relabelling is a (q+1)-st root of unity mod 𝔪
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q \neq 2$ and $5 \le q$ (`hq2`, `hq`), a prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$ (`hℓ3`), a nonzero natural number $M'$, and a commutative ring $A_0$.
--
--   **Invariance of the level structures.** The hypothesis `hℓ` says that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, every Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, every variable change $C$ and every `LevelPData` $D$ over $T$ (a quadruple $x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q$ of elements of $T$), the predicate `IsLevelPStructure W ℓ D` — both pairs satisfy the affine Weierstrass equation of $W$, $x_P$ and $x_Q$ are roots of $W.\mathrm{pre}\Psi_\ell$, and the two elements $\mathrm{indepElt}(W,\ell,x_P,x_Q)$, $\mathrm{indepElt}(W,\ell,x_Q,x_P)$ are units — implies `IsLevelPStructure (C • W) ℓ (D.variableChange C)`. The hypothesis `hM` says that `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h` (for $p^k = 2$ the two-torsion-kernel condition on $h$, otherwise the cyclic-kernel-generator condition: degree at most $\varphi(p^k)/2$, leading coefficient $1$, $h\cdot\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^{k-1}} \mid \mathrm{pre}\Psi_{p^k}$, and the divisibility of the relevant scaled numerators) is preserved by $C$ together with the substitution `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k)` on $h$.
--
--   **Group laws, transport and graded realisations.** $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws A₀`, assigning to every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and every projective Weierstrass model over $T$ with unit discriminant a relative group law on its projective model; `h𝒢` states that each such law is of chord–tangent type (it admits a points-evaluation), and `h𝒢O` that its identity section is cut out by a ring homomorphism from the origin chart ring killing $x/y$ and $z/y$. $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q`, i.e. functorial transport of raw Drinfeld pairs (a projective curve with two sections) along $A_0$-algebra maps and along variable changes, preserving the condition that the pair is a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ for $\mathcal G$; `h𝒯` states that this transport is compatible with the induced morphisms of projective models (`IsSectionTransport`). Further, `hℓA` requires $\ell$ to be a unit in $A_0$, while `hVC` and `hCO` require, for every base and every variable change resp. every $A_0$-algebra map of bases, the existence of a graded ring homomorphism between the graded coordinate rings of the projective models which dominates the irrelevant ideal and satisfies `IsVariableChangeHom` resp. `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   **The moduli problem and its universal object.** Let $\mathcal R :=$ `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯`, the rigid Weierstrass data attached to the product of three level components: the $\Gamma_0$-power component (a family of polynomials indexed by the prime factors of $M'$, each satisfying `IsGamma0PowAt` at the corresponding exponent in the factorisation of $M'$), the level-$\ell$ component (`LevelPData` with `IsLevelPStructure`), and the Drinfeld component of level $q$ for $\mathcal G$. A raw object over $T$ thus consists of a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a triple `level` whose parts are written `level.1`, `level.2.1`, `level.2.2`, and $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}\,T$ is the quotient of raw objects by variable change. $P_0$ is a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for the associated level moduli datum: an $A_0$-algebra $B_0 = P_0.B_0$ with a point `P₀.univ` over $B_0$ such that every point over every $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of `P₀.univ` under a unique $A_0$-algebra map $B_0 \to T$; `P₀.classify` denotes that unique map. Finally $x$ is a raw object over $B_0$ whose class is `P₀.univ` (`hx`).
--
--   **The local ring and its residue data.** $R$ is a Noetherian local domain, complete for the topology of its maximal ideal, an $A_0$-algebra, and $\iota : B_0 \to R$ is an $A_0$-algebra map. $k$ is a field of characteristic $q$ in which $\ell$ and $M'$ are nonzero (`hℓk`, `hM'k`), and $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ is a surjective ring homomorphism with kernel the maximal ideal (`hresR`, `hkerR`). $W_0$ is a complete discrete valuation domain with maximal ideal generated by $q$ (`hW₀`) and surjection $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ with kernel the maximal ideal (`hres₀`, `hker₀`); $R$ is a $W_0$-algebra, $W_0$ an $A_0$-algebra, the tower is compatible, and $\mathrm{res}_R \circ (\text{structure map } W_0 \to R) = \mathrm{res}_0$ (`hresR₀`). The hypothesis `hfac` expresses that $(R,\iota)$ is universal among Artinian local test objects: for every Artinian local $W_0$- and $A_0$-algebra $T$ in the tower, with surjection $\mathrm{res}_T : T \to k$ of kernel the maximal ideal compatible with $\mathrm{res}_0$, and every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi : B_0 \to T$ whose reduction agrees with $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \iota$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\Phi : R \to T$ compatible with the residue maps and satisfying $\Phi \circ \iota = \varphi$.
--
--   **Formal groups and the Drinfeld basis.** $F$ is a commutative formal group over $R$ whose power series is the fixed formal group law of the curve of $(\mathcal R.\mathrm{mapRing}\ \iota\ x).\mathrm{level}.2.2$ (`hFW`), and $F_0$ a commutative formal group over $k$ whose power series is that of the reduction of this curve along $\mathrm{res}_R$ (`hF₀W`), with `hF₀` asserting `F₀.IsDrinfeldBasisAdic ⊥ q 0 0`: relative to the zero ideal, the $q$-th series of $F_0$ is a unit multiple of its Drinfeld divisor at $(0,0)$. The hypothesis `hssJ` asserts that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\iota_\Omega : k \to \Omega$, the image of $\mathrm{res}_R(\iota(P_0.j_0))$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), that is, every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Moreover $\chi_P,\chi_Q$ are ring homomorphisms from the origin chart ring of that curve to $R$ such that the sections $P$ and $Q$ of the Drinfeld component reduce to the origin through them (`hP`, `hQ`: each $\chi$ is an origin chart section for the given section and both $\mathrm{originParam}\,\chi = -\chi(x/y)$ and $\mathrm{originW}\,\chi$ lie in the maximal ideal); `hBC` says $F_0$ is the base change of $F$ along $\mathrm{res}_R$; `hDr` says $F$ is a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ at the parameters $\mathrm{originParam}\,\chi_P$, $\mathrm{originParam}\,\chi_Q$ for the maximal-ideal topology; `hmax` says the maximal ideal of $R$ is generated by these two parameters. The hypothesis `huniv` is the corresponding universal property of $(R,F)$ as a deformation ring with Drinfeld level structure: for every Artinian local $W_0$-algebra $T$ with compatible surjection $\mathrm{res}_T$ onto $k$ of kernel the maximal ideal, every commutative formal group $G$ over $T$ base-changing to $F_0$, and every pair $y_0,y_1$ in the maximal ideal of $T$ making $G$ a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ at $(y_0,y_1)$, there is a unique $W_0$-algebra map $\varphi : R \to T$ compatible with the residue maps for which there exist a formal group $F'$ over $T$ which is the base change of $F$ along $\varphi$ and a law isomorphism $\psi : F' \to G$ whose series reduces to the identity series ($\mathrm{res}_T$ of the $n$-th coefficient is $1$ for $n = 1$ and $0$ otherwise) and which carries $\varphi(\mathrm{originParam}\,\chi_P)$ to $y_0$ and $\varphi(\mathrm{originParam}\,\chi_Q)$ to $y_1$ under its adic evaluation.
--
--   **The relabelling.** $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lies in $\Gamma_0(M')$ (`hγ`), and $\rho_\gamma$ is an automorphism of the moduli problem (a family of self-maps of the point sets, natural in the base and preserving the $j$-invariant). The hypothesis `hpin` pins $\rho_\gamma$ down on fields: for every field $T$ that is an $A_0$-algebra and raw objects $y,y'$ over $T$ with the discriminant of $y.\mathrm{level}.2.2.\mathrm{curve}$ a unit, if $y'$ has the same curve as $y$, the same $\Gamma_0$-component, level-$\ell$ data obtained from that of $y$ by the relabelling of `LevelRelabelling.LevelPData.relabel` with the integer matrix of $\gamma$ (replacing $(P,Q)$ by $(\gamma_{00}P+\gamma_{10}Q,\ \gamma_{01}P+\gamma_{11}Q)$ for the group law on the affine curve), and Drinfeld pair obtained from that of $y$ by the corresponding integral linear combinations of the two sections for the group law $\mathcal G$, then $\rho_\gamma$ sends the class of $y$ to the class of $y'$. The hypothesis `hfix` states that for every $b \in B_0$ the element $\iota(P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma.\mathrm{act}\ P_0.\mathrm{univ})\,b) - \iota(b)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R$, and $\theta_0 : R \to R$ is a $W_0$-algebra endomorphism which realises this classifying map on $B_0$, i.e. $\theta_0(\iota b) = \iota(P_0.\mathrm{classify}(\rho_\gamma.\mathrm{act}\ P_0.\mathrm{univ})\,b)$ for all $b$ (`hcompl`), and which is congruent to the identity modulo the maximal ideal (`hres`).
--
--   Finally $V$ is a variable change over $R$, the discriminant of the curve of $(\mathcal R.\mathrm{mapRing}\ \iota\ x).\mathrm{level}.2.2$ is a unit (`hΔ`), and $x'$ is a raw object over $R$ with: $x' = V \cdot \bigl(\mathcal R.\mathrm{mapRing}\ \theta_0\ (\mathcal R.\mathrm{mapRing}\ \iota\ x)\bigr)$, where $\theta_0$ is viewed as an $A_0$-algebra map (`hact`); the same curve as $\mathcal R.\mathrm{mapRing}\ \iota\ x$ (`hcurve`); the same $\Gamma_0$-component (`hlev1`); Drinfeld pair equal to the $\gamma$-relabelling of that of $\mathcal R.\mathrm{mapRing}\ \iota\ x$ (`hlev22`); and level-$\ell$ data which, after passage to the fraction field of $R$, equals the $\gamma$-relabelling over that field of the level-$\ell$ data of $\mathcal R.\mathrm{mapRing}\ \iota\ x$ (`hlev21`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Writing $u \in R$ for the image of the unit $V.u \in R^\times$, the following three assertions hold:
--
--   1. $u^{q+1} - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R$;
--
--   2. if $\gamma \in \Gamma(\ell)$, then $u - 1$ lies in the maximal ideal of $R$;
--
--   3. if $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\gamma \notin \Gamma(\ell)$, then $u - 1$ does not lie in the maximal ideal of $R$.
--
--   This is the scalar part of the analysis of how a $\Gamma_0(M')$-relabelling acts on the universal deformation ring with Drinfeld level-$q$ structure at a supersingular point: the unit scaling of the variable change which realises the relabelling reduces, modulo the maximal ideal, to a $(q+1)$-st root of unity, and its reduction is trivial precisely in the $\Gamma(\ell)$-trivial case (in the presence of $\Gamma(q)$-triviality). It is used in the construction of the linear part of the relabelling on the Drinfeld parameters, [`ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_originParam_linearPart_of_algHom_comp_eq_classify_act_of_problemAut_relabel_gamma0Pow_of_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.LevelModuliPackageAbs.exists_originParam_linearPart_of_algHom_comp_eq_classify_act_of_problemAut_relabel_gamma0Pow_of_mem_ssJSet).
